-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_addmodulepath.pcpp - Directive compliance: @addmodulepath

  @addmodulepath "<folder>"; adds a folder where import looks for units
  (BNF.md sec 1 and 2). The folder must exist; only the main module sets it.
  import looks in the importing file's own folder first, then in the module
  paths in the order they were added; every imported unit searches the same
  list. One folder named again (in any spelling) is the same folder.

  This program adds res\tests\libs twice, in two spellings, and imports:
    dir_addmodulepath_lib      only in res\tests\libs: found through the path
    dir_addmodulepath_unit     beside this file; it imports dir_addmodulepath_lib
                               too, through the main module's path
    dir_addmodulepath_shadow   in both folders: the copy beside this file wins
                               (Folder() = 1; the libs copy returns 2)

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addmodulepath.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addmodulepath.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    dir_addmodulepath_lib.Value() = 40
    dir_addmodulepath_unit.FromUnit() = 41
    dir_addmodulepath_shadow.Folder() = 1
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  Both targets print the same; the [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // ERROR / WARN / HINT comment on its marked line says,
  and nothing else:
    dir_addmodulepath_err_missing.pcpp   a folder that does not exist
    dir_addmodulepath_err_file.pcpp      a file, not a folder
    dir_addmodulepath_err_path.pcpp      a path no file routine can take
    dir_addmodulepath_err_unit.pcpp      the directive in an imported unit
                                         (dir_addmodulepath_err_unit_unit.pcpp)
    dir_addmodulepath_err_nopath.pcpp    dir_addmodulepath_lib imported without
                                         @addmodulepath
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addmodulepath;
@addmodulepath "$P:res/tests/libs";
@addmodulepath "$P:res\\tests\\libs\\";
import dir_addmodulepath_unit, dir_addmodulepath_lib, dir_addmodulepath_shadow;

begin
  println("dir_addmodulepath_lib.Value() = {}", dir_addmodulepath_lib.Value());
  println("dir_addmodulepath_unit.FromUnit() = {}", dir_addmodulepath_unit.FromUnit());
  println("dir_addmodulepath_shadow.Folder() = {}", dir_addmodulepath_shadow.Folder());
end.
